  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensuring Evidence-Based and Coordinated Durable Solutions Planning and Promoting Social Cohesion and Peace Building between Internally Displaced Persons and Host Communities in the Boeny Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project supports the GIZ initiative &quot;Improving the management of internal migration in the context of climate change in host communities (PROMIC)&quot; in the Boeny region of Madagascar. It addresses the challenges posed by climate-induced internal migration, which has strained local resources and heightened tensions between Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) and host communities. With over 108,000 individuals displaced from southern Madagascar between 2019 and 2022, Boeny has become a major destination, overwhelming local authorities and causing social conflicts. By enhancing understanding of migration patterns and root causes of conflicts and fragility through tools like tand Solutions and Mobility Index (SMI), the project aims to inform long-term planning and policy-making to foster durable solution for migrants and host communities in the region. Key activities include training on SMI tools, data collection, publishing reports, and capacity-building for national and local authorities to strengthen their data management and response capabilities. The project ultimately seeks to improve social cohesion, resilience, and sustainable management of natural resources in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
